---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Generate a static, offline documentation site from the workspace

Usage: rustman docs build [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --out <DIR>
          Output folder; only files a previous build wrote are replaced
          
          [default: site]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format
          
          [default: html]
          [possible values: html, markdown, both]

      --env <NAME>
          Environment whose [docs].publish_variables values are shown (default: none)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --examples <EXAMPLES>
          Where opted-in examples come from
          
          [default: history]
          [possible values: history, snapshot]

      --force
          Write into a non-empty folder that rustman docs did not generate

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
